        <detaileddescription>
<para>Construct a child edge that belongs to the specified parent.</para><para>When constructing a class containing a data member of this type (i.e., a tree edge that points to a child of this vertex), the data member must be initialized by passing <computeroutput>*this</computeroutput> as the argument. See the example in this class documentation.</para><para>An optional second argument initializes the child pointer for the edge. The initialization is the same as if the child had been assigned with <computeroutput>operator=</computeroutput> later. I.e., the child must not already have a parent. </para>        </detaileddescription>
